Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Override `OnBackButtonPressed` on your page

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget the async confirmation
            Dispatcher.Dispatch(async () =>
            {
                bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                    "Unsaved Changes",
                    "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                    "Discard", "Stay");

                if (leave)
                    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
            });

            return true; // Cancel the default back navigation
        }

        return base.OnBackButtonPressed(); // Allow normal navigation
    }
}
```

Returning `true` from `OnBackButtonPressed` cancels the hardware/software back button.

## 2. Custom "Cancel" toolbar button

In your XAML, replace the default back arrow with a Cancel button:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource CancelBackButton}">

    <ContentPage.Resources>
        <BackButtonBehavior x:Key="CancelBackButton"
                            TextOverride="Cancel"
                            Command="{Binding CancelCommand}" />
    </ContentPage.Resources>
    <!-- ... -->
</ContentPage>
```

Or set it directly:

```xml
<Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
    <BackButtonBehavior TextOverride="Cancel"
                        Command="{Binding CancelCommand}" />
</Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
```

## 3. ViewModel command with confirmation

```csharp
[RelayCommand]
private async Task Cancel()
{
    if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
    {
        bool leave = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
            "Unsaved Changes",
            "Discard changes?",
            "Discard", "Stay");

        if (!leave) return;
    }

    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
}
```

## Key points

| Concern | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Hardware back (Android) | `OnBackButtonPressed()` → return `true` to cancel |
| Shell back arrow | `BackButtonBehavior` with custom `Command` (bypasses default nav) |
| Custom text | `BackButtonBehavior.TextOverride` |
| iOS swipe-back | Set `IsEnabled="False"` on `BackButtonBehavior` to disable the gesture |

> **Note:** `BackButtonBehavior.Command` replaces the default navigation entirely — Shell won't navigate back automatically when a command is set, so you control it fully.
